rav-audio - SalonRPI audio box
==============================

Audio path: MPD and Bluetooth A2DP -> PipeWire (user mpd, lingering
user manager) -> default output. The visualizer (audio-visualizer.service,
/usr/bin/rav-visualizer) captures that output's monitor passively, so the
output still suspends when nothing plays.

Default output (WirePlumber priorities): an I2S DAC such as a HifiBerry
when its overlay is enabled, else the onboard headphone jack, then HDMI.

Shipped (conffiles, kept across upgrades):
  /etc/rav-audio/mpd.conf                      MPD config (MPDCONF), local
                                               additions in mpd_local.conf
  /etc/pipewire/pipewire.conf.d/10-rav-audio.conf
  /etc/wireplumber/wireplumber.conf.d/50-rav-audio.conf

Generated by postinst (depend on the uid of mpd), removed with the package:
  /etc/systemd/system/mpd.service.d/50-rav-audio-runtime.conf
  /etc/systemd/system/audio-visualizer.service.d/50-rav-audio-runtime.conf
  /etc/systemd/system/user@<mpd uid>.service.d/50-rav-audio-runtime.conf

postinst also enables linger for mpd, disables bluealsa (re-enabled on
removal if it was enabled), sets Class/AlwaysPairable/... in
/etc/bluetooth/main.conf (left in place on removal) and creates
/etc/bluetooth/pin.conf with a random PIN if missing.

Not handled: config.txt needs dtparam=spi=on (OLEDs) and an audio output,
dtoverlay=hifiberry-... or dtparam=audio=on (postinst only warns).

Inspect the audio graph:
  sudo -u mpd XDG_RUNTIME_DIR=/run/user/$(id -u mpd) wpctl status
